--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Portions derived from aqua-rs-sdk
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project incorporates material from the Aqua Protocol Rust SDK
("aqua-rs-sdk"), Copyright inblock.io assets GmbH, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

1. Name validation rules (src/name.rs)

   The registry name validation and normalization logic in `src/name.rs` is
   a port of `aqua-rs-sdk/src/registry/name.rs`. The rules (NFC
   normalization, Unicode script isolation, allowed character categories,
   the 64 and 128 scalar length caps, and Latin case folding) implement
   section 3.3 of the Aqua Protocol type registry specification, and are
   reproduced faithfully so that names resolve identically in both
   implementations. Divergence would silently break name resolution
   compatibility.

2. Registration template definitions (src/templates/*.json)

   The three registration template definitions

       src/templates/vendor_registration.json
       src/templates/template_registration.json
       src/templates/alias_registration.json

   are byte-identical copies of the corresponding files in
   `aqua-rs-sdk/src/schema/templates/`. They are vendored rather than
   depended upon because `aqua-rs-sdk-core`, this project's only runtime
   dependency on the SDK family, deliberately ships no registration
   templates.

   A template's hash is its type identity, so these files must never be
   reformatted, re-indented, or otherwise modified. The tests in
   `tests/cross_sdk.rs` assert that the hashes computed from these copies
   equal the constants `VendorRegistration::TEMPLATE_LINK`,
   `TemplateRegistration::TEMPLATE_LINK`, and
   `AliasRegistration::TEMPLATE_LINK` in aqua-rs-sdk.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Specification
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The behavior implemented here follows the Aqua Protocol specifications:

    extensions/spec-type-registry.md     (sections 3 and 8)
    extensions/spec-module-ecosystem.md  (sections 7, 8, and 11)
